{{/*
family: web-ui
what: trap
transports: v2c, v3
reference: RFC 3416 (SNMPv2 notifications), RFC 3414 (SNMPv3 users)
verification: reference
*/}}
{{define "does"}}The values to enter in the device's SNMP trap (notification) page so it sends traps to Woodshed (SNMP{{.Transport}}).{{end}}

{{define "parts"}}
@@part steps - In the device's web page, open its SNMP trap or notification settings and add a receiver
Trap receiver (manager) address: {{.Address}}
Port: {{.Port}}
SNMP version: {{if eq .Transport "v2c"}}v2c{{else}}v3{{end}}
{{- if eq .Transport "v2c"}}
Community: <COMMUNITY>
{{- else}}
User name: {{.V3User}}
Security level: authentication and privacy (authPriv)
Authentication: {{.Auth.Label}}, passphrase <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
Privacy: {{.Priv.Label}}, passphrase <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
{{- end}}
Notification type: trap (not inform), unless the page offers informs and you want them answered
{{end}}

{{define "notes"}}
{{if eq .Transport "v2c"}}<COMMUNITY> must be one Woodshed accepts: Settings → Listeners → SNMP traps lists the communities (an empty list accepts any).
{{else}}Add the same user in Woodshed: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, with the same name, protocols and passphrases.
{{end}}
Field names differ between devices. Many pages also ask which events send a trap.
{{end}}

{{define "check"}}Search Events for type Traps after saving; pages with a "send test trap" button send one at once.{{end}}
